---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { recipeExamples, exampleHref } from '../lib/recipe-examples';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import '../styles/practical-labs.css';
const architecturePages=[['rag','RAG'],['knowledge-graphs','Knowledge graphs'],['single-agent','Single agent'],['agent-harness','Agent harness'],['agentic-rag','Agentic RAG'],['human-in-the-loop','Human approval'],['agent-teammates','Always-on assistants']];
const threads=[['graph-engineering','Graph engineering'],['what-the-model-sees','What the model sees'],['who-approves-what','Who approves what'],['checking-the-work','Checking the work']];
---
<Base title="Resource quality prototype · Review" description="Review the proposed diagrams, practical recipe examples, technical corrections, and evidence before publication.">
 <div class="page-hero lab-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Private review · September 21, 2026</div><h1>Clearer models.<br/>More useful examples.</h1><p>This prototype strengthens the explanation, then connects it to something you can run and inspect. The live site is unchanged.</p><div class="review-actions"><a class="lab-button" href={url('/recipes/document-qa/#try-with-your-ai')}>Try a recipe with your AI ↗</a><a href={url('/')}>Explore the prototype homepage →</a></div></div>
 <div class="review-stats"><div><strong>7</strong><span>Rebuilt architecture diagrams</span></div><div><strong>6</strong><span>Recipes with copyable examples</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>Revised cross-cutting explanations</span></div><div><strong>8</strong><span>Design decisions explained</span></div></div>
 <section class="lab-section"><div class="eyebrow">A short review route</div><h2>Start with these three changes.</h2><div class="review-route"><a href={url('/techniques/rag/')}><span>01 / Understand</span><h3>Read the new RAG diagram.</h3><p>Indexing and query-time retrieval are distinct, arrows say what they carry, and the explanation separates evidence selection from answer correctness.</p></a><a href={url('/recipes/incident-runbook/#try-with-your-ai')}><span>02 / Apply</span><h3>Inspect a bounded incident agent.</h3><p>A real model can choose read-only tools, inspect their results, and hand back an evidence-backed hypothesis within a fixed call budget.</p></a><a href={url('/design-decisions/')}><span>03 / Go deeper</span><h3>Compare the design decisions.</h3><p>Reasoning, context, teams, tools, durability, and evaluation—what each changes, what it does not establish, and what to measure.</p></a></div></section>
 <section class="lab-section" id="changes"><div class="eyebrow">Complete change list</div><h2>What changed in this prototype</h2>
  <ol class="review-changes">
   <li><h3>Seven architecture diagrams rebuilt</h3><p>Named connectors, distinct information and control paths, visible completion and refusal paths where relevant, model highlighting, readable node detail, and nearby legends. On phones, a connected reading view preserves every labeled relationship without shrinking a desktop graphic.</p><div class="review-links">{architecturePages.map(([slug,title])=><a href={url(`/techniques/${slug}/`)}>{title} ↗</a>)}</div></li>
   <li><h3>Shared diagram presentation improved</h3><p>The remaining concept diagrams gain wrapped detail text, stronger heading hierarchy, more consistent framing, and an expandable list of connections in words. These are presentation improvements; those diagrams have not all been replaced with bespoke architectures.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Three new visual comparisons under “Follow an idea”</h3><p>Context versus memory versus checkpoints; proposal versus authorization versus execution; and record validity versus outcome quality versus tracing. The existing graph-engineering comparison remains beside its revised explanation.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Four thread explanations tightened and corrected</h3><p>Removed claims that agent graphs need no advance design, all graphs checkpoint after every node, memory selection belongs only at level 7, or separate reviewers are inherently independent. Explained hybrid workflows, optional human gates, evaluation of single runs, and implementation-dependent persistence.</p><div class="review-links">{threads.map(([slug,title])=><a href={url(`/threads/${slug}/`)}>{title} ↗</a>)}</div></li>
   <li><h3>Three technique explanations corrected</h3><p>Agent graphs now distinguish mechanism from framework features. Always-on assistants no longer require a dedicated computer or a model call on every timer tick. Evaluations now include code, human, and model graders rather than a false two-way choice.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Eight architecture decisions made explicit</h3><p>A new guide covers the nuances, tradeoffs, failure modes, and measurements behind common choices. Primary sources are linked beside each topic. The levels are explicitly an editorial framework, not a universal standard or required progression.</p><a href={url('/design-decisions/')}>Read design decisions →</a></li>
   <li><h3>Six practical examples folded into Recipes</h3><p>Each recipe now offers a copyable brief with sample inputs and review criteria. Reference answers, design detail, failure cases, and adaptation guidance expand when needed. Companion variations are explicitly distinguished from the larger recipe.</p><div class="review-links">{recipeExamples.map(l=><a href={url(exampleHref(l))}>{l.title} ↗</a>)}</div></li>
   <li><h3>Implementation remains optional</h3><p>Python downloads sit inside a closed “Optional” disclosure. Each includes editable data, a task brief, the expected reference, a standard-library Python runner, a README, and offline tests. The shared runner supports local Ollama and compatible Chat Completions endpoints. Offline replay and live generation are separately labeled.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Real control behavior implemented</h3><p>Lexical retrieval with source IDs; extraction checks and arithmetic; a validated two-call reporting workflow; a version-bound approval simulation; an allowlisted read-only agent loop; and a persistent SQLite outbox with duplicate-event handling. These are teaching implementations, with production omissions stated.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Worked examples made directly readable</h3><p>The shared walkthrough opens immediately. Removed the pretend “Send request” step and typewriter animation. Readers can inspect any stage, while changed-condition exercises and approval simulations remain available.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Navigation and model-readable access connected</h3><p>Removed the separate Labs section, its navigation item, and homepage promotion. Concept links and search now lead directly into the relevant recipes. Recipe Markdown exports include the practical material.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Prototype review and validation kept visible</h3><p>A banner links back here from every page. Source and output records distinguish authored examples from observed model behavior. The prototype stays in an isolated checkout and is served privately for review.</p></li>
   <li><h3>Repository validation updated</h3><p>Integrated the recipe exports and example runner with the existing validators. Corrected the timeline’s aggregate checked date to match its latest recorded source check; milestone assignments and dates are unchanged. The complete notes identify remaining pre-existing test failures.</p></li>
  </ol>
 </section>
 <section class="lab-section"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence and limits</div><h2>What the checks establish</h2><div class="lab-intro"><div><b>Implementation checks</b><p>The build, type checks, existing site tests, new diagram invariants, and offline example tests cover structure and behavior. Local-model smoke trials exercise the API adapter and task paths using synthetic inputs. Failed trials are retained.</p><a href={url('/downloads/quality-validation.json')}>Inspect recorded model trials ↗</a></div><div><b>What remains to establish</b><p>This is not a claim that every page is current or that these designs outperform alternatives. It does not reverify the entire product registry, benchmark multiple models, replace every diagram, or substitute for reader testing. The legacy scripted cases remain authored illustrations.</p></div></div><p>The complete review notes include technical changes, checks, local-model findings, and remaining work.</p><a href={url('/downloads/quality-prototype-notes.md')} download>Download the complete change log ↓</a></section>
</Base>
<style>.review-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px;font-size:13px}.review-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:28px 0}.review-stats strong{display:block;font:500 38px var(--font);letter-spacing:-1px;margin-bottom:5px}.review-stats span{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.review-route{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}.review-route a{display:block;padding:24px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;text-decoration:none}.review-route a:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}.review-route span{font-size:10px;color:var(--accent)}.review-route h3{margin:16px 0 10px;font-size:20px}.review-route p{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8}.review-changes{padding-left:24px;max-width:1000px}.review-changes>li{padding:20px 0 24px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.review-changes>li::marker{font-size:12px;color:var(--accent)}.review-changes p{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.review-changes a{font-size:12px;color:var(--accent)}.review-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 20px;margin-top:14px}.lab-intro a{display:block;margin-top:12px;color:var(--accent);font-size:12px}@media(max-width:760px){.review-route{grid-template-columns:1fr}.review-stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.review-changes{padding-left:16px}.review-changes>li{padding-left:4px}}</style>
